# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/prefill-3 window (the masked tail pass of a prompt as a trace replay; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/prefill-3 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-pf3-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-pf3-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a NEW tag in every template (a rebuild under an existing tag keeps the old image). This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a smoke job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory; the keys are the same
# in every smoke job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone. The prefix steps (AP1, R1, R2) do not forward the selection into their container and serve the base checkpoint: a tail pass
# replays the same traces on either.
# L2 (ARENA LADDER, 80 MB; information): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-pf3-s5-a80, the timed arm with the arena at 80 MB. The attach is the measurement: it
# passes when the engaged line says uncovered=0 and the arena came back at its address, and it fails BY NAME (the hole census) when the arena is smaller than what the
# captures used. The smallest rung that passes is the arena a ship profile would carry; each megabyte of it is DRAM the eager chunk loop does not have. A failed rung is the
# answer, not a halt. the lines in the container log: "[PINDIAG] lever N route installed: ... tailtrace=traced" once; on the arms "[PINDIAG] prefill tail trace engaged
# buckets=.. traces=<n> sink=<id> taps=5,19,33,47,61 arena_mb=<mb> arena_address=.. freed=<k> uncovered=0 capture_ms=.." once and one "[PF3] tail mode=traced bucket=..
# valid=.. start=.. ms=.. stage_ms=.. replay_ms=.." per traced tail pass; on the control one "[PF3] tail mode=eager bucket=.. valid=.. start=.. ms=.." per tail pass below
# the 2,048-row bucket and no "engaged" line; no "fell back" line, no "[PF3] tail skip" line that the control would not also take (a skip is a call that ran the stock pass:
# vision, an untraced bucket, another page-table width, another tap set) and no program growth after the warm anywhere CHECKPOINT READ (the workflow passes
# c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a key=...
# weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)" once, a "weight cache ...: found" line (the cache the Swift window built; this
# pack never builds it) and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line; the models answer names ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. Duration (estimate): 30 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-pf3-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-pf3-s5-a80
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=60
